  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "small bore piping was not specifically analyzed for vulnerability of fatigue failure due to operational or resonance vibration...this branch line was erroneously excluded from further evaluation. Additionally, during EPU evaluations the small bore piping was considered rigid in the seismic calculation and was not evaluated independently from the large bore piping...the design calculation failed to identify that the stress caused by flow induced resonance vibration at Recirculation System Pump speeds between 1500 and 1600 rpm was sufficient to exceed the endurance limit for the failed pipe assembly.",
